  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759988,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 18 Years Mercury: A Commodore 64 Chronicle\n\n**18 Years Mercury** plunges players into a chillingly familiar world, eighteen years after the fall of Big Brother in George Orwell's *1984*. While the telescreens are gone and the Thought Police disbanded, the scars of Oceania’s totalitarian regime run deep.  A fragile, nascent democracy struggles to take root, threatened by lingering paranoia, black market activity, and the insidious resurgence of old ideologies.\n\nYou play as Elias Thorne, a former Party member seeking redemption and uncovering a conspiracy that reaches into the highest echelons of the new government. Navigate the decaying urban landscapes of London, now a sprawling maze of abandoned factories and makeshift settlements.  \n\nThis atmospheric adventure combines exploration, puzzle-solving, and tense stealth sequences.  Gather clues, interact with a cast of morally ambiguous characters, and make choices that shape Elias's journey and the fate of Oceania.  Featuring a haunting soundtrack and detailed pixel art, *18 Years Mercury* explores themes of memory, truth, and the enduring power of hope in a world struggling to rebuild.  Can Elias expose the truth before the shadows of the past consume the future?"
    },
